<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="page-header">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Community Guidelines</div>
  <h1>Community Guidelines</h1>
  <p>Our shared rules for a respectful, helpful, and inclusive language-learning community.</p>
</div>

<article class="guidelines-content">

  <section class="guideline-section">
    <h2>1. Be Respectful</h2>
    <p>
      Treat every member with kindness and respect, regardless of their language level, nationality, or background.
      Language learning is challenging — encourage beginners, celebrate progress, and offer constructive feedback
      rather than criticism.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guideline-section">
    <h2>2. Stay On Topic</h2>
    <p>
      Post discussions in the appropriate language category. Threads should relate to language learning, linguistics,
      literature, or cultural topics associated with the language. Off-topic posts may be moved or removed by moderators.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guideline-section">
    <h2>3. Attribute Sources and References</h2>
    <p>
      When sharing information from external sources — textbooks, websites, academic articles, or other
      publications — always provide proper attribution. Include the author, title, and URL or publication details.
      Plagiarism and copyright infringement are not tolerated.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guideline-section">
    <h2>4. No Spam or Self-Promotion</h2>
    <p>
      Do not post unsolicited advertising, affiliate links, or repeated self-promotional content.
      Sharing genuinely helpful resources (courses, tools, books) is welcome when relevant and disclosed honestly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guideline-section">
    <h2>5. Use Clear and Accessible Language</h2>
    <p>
      The forum welcomes learners at all levels. When writing complex explanations, consider using examples and
      breaking down jargon. If your post includes content in a language other than English, please provide a brief
      translation or summary to keep discussions inclusive.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guideline-section">
    <h2>6. No Hate Speech or Discrimination</h2>
    <p>
      Content that demeans, discriminates against, or harasses any individual or group based on language, nationality,
      ethnicity, religion, gender, or any other characteristic is strictly prohibited and will result in immediate
      removal and account suspension.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guideline-section">
    <h2>7. Report Violations</h2>
    <p>
      If you see content that violates these guidelines, please flag it for moderator review. Do not engage with
      rule-breaking posts — report them and move on. Community moderation depends on all of us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guideline-section">
    <h2>8. Privacy and Safety</h2>
    <p>
      Do not share personal information about yourself or others — including real names, addresses, or contact details.
      Use a display name that does not identify you personally unless you choose to do so.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guideline-section guideline-section--callout">
    <h2>A Note on Language and Culture</h2>
    <p>
      Languages are living expressions of culture, history, and identity. Approach discussions about languages and
      their communities with curiosity and humility. There are no "better" or "worse" languages — only different
      ones, each with its own richness.
    </p>
  </section>

</article>

<div class="cta-bar">
  <p>Ready to join the conversation?</p>
  <a href="/threads/new" class="btn btn-primary">Start a Discussion</a>
  <a href="/categories" class="btn btn-outline">Browse Categories</a>
</div>

